    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44978" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sphaerĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφαιρικός</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a ball</i>, <i>spherical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">motus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2, 14, 31</span></i>
			: numeri, Boëth. <i><span class="en">Inst. Arith.
				2, 4</span></i>.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sphaerĭca</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>spherics</i>, <i>the science of heavenly motions</i>,
			Boëth. <i><span class="en">Inst. Arith. 1, 1, p.
			11</span></i>.</div>
